{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Interface profiles for the channel check. Values per line (differential channels are computed in the odd mode: r = half the differential resistance). Source 'kind': spec = from the standard or a source close to it, guideline = vendor layout guideline, kisi = kisi's own guide value without a standard behind it. Traffic-light limits: eye_h_* as a fraction of the transmit swing, eye_w_min_ui in UI, skew_ps intra-pair skew (null = 5 % UI), rl_min_db up to 1.5 × Nyquist, stub_factor = via stub resonance must lie above stub_factor × Nyquist, il_board_db = loss of the board section at Nyquist (null = no limit). This file can be extended without code changes. Order = priority of the automatic assignment (net name before class name, first matching profile). Pin capacitances and driver resistances are typical estimates; replace them with the part's IBIS data.",
  "defaults": {
    "limits": {
      "eye_h_red": 0.4,
      "eye_h_yellow": 0.65,
      "eye_w_min_ui": 0.5,
      "skew_ps": null,
      "rl_min_db": 10,
      "stub_factor": 2,
      "il_board_db": null
    },
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "kisi",
        "text": "Traffic-light limits for eye, return loss and stub resonance are kisi guide values for a board without equalisation, not values from a standard."
      }
    ]
  },
  "profiles": [
